  "final_message": "**Status:** Reproduced\n\nNo production code was changed. The only additions are the test and fixtures listed under Artifacts.\n\n**Expected:** In `SubComponent`, `<template #_duration>` content from `App.vue` replaces the slot's fallback content, the same way `<template #title>` does (and the same as 3.5.13).\n\n**Actual:** `title` renders the passed content, but `_duration` renders the red default slot content (\"This is the default slot content for `_duration`...\"):\n\n```\n<div><p>...</p><div style=\"color: green;\">`title` template works</div><div style=\"color: red;\">This is the default slot content for `_duration`.<br>...</div></div>\n```\n\n**Trigger:** Both of these are needed:\n- An underscore-prefixed slot name on the inner component (`#_duration`).\n- A sibling `<template v-if=\"...\" #someSlot>` next to the inner component in `BaseLayout`'s slot content, which makes `BaseLayout`'s slots dynamic (`_: 2`).\n\nFour variants from the reporter's files all pass, so each condition is necessary. I removed them afterwards. They were:\n- the sibling template without `v-if`\n- the slot renamed without the underscore\n- no sibling template at all\n- a plain `<p v-if>` as the sibling\n\n**Run:** from the repo root:\n```\npnpm exec vitest run --config vitest.unit.config.ts packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName.spec.ts\n```\nIt exits 1 now. It failed 10/10 runs, so it is deterministic. It asserts only that both `title` and `_duration` render their template content and not their fallback content.\n\n**Passes when:**\n- The same unmodified spec, run against published `vue@3.5.13` (runtime and `compiler-sfc`) with a throwaway config in /tmp, passes (exit 0).\n- Against published 3.5.14 and 3.5.17 it fails with the same assertion, which matches the report's version range.\n- In this checkout, a throwaway one-line patch passes (exit 0). I reverted it. The patch changed `assignSlots` in `packages/runtime-core/src/componentSlots.ts` from `!isInternalKey(key)` back to `key !== '_'`.\n\n**Likely cause (pointer only):** `assignSlots` skips every slot key starting with `_` when `optimized` is false. 3.5.13 skipped only the exact key `_`.\n\n**Artifacts:**\n- `/work/runs/6e221d71d0/repo/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName.spec.ts` compiles the `.vue` files with the in-repo `@vue/compiler-sfc`, mounts `App` in jsdom and asserts.\n- `/work/runs/6e221d71d0/repo/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName/` holds the reporter's `App.vue`, `BaseLayout.vue` and `SubComponent.vue`, decoded unmodified from the playground link.\n",
  "run_command": "pnpm exec vitest run --config vitest.unit.config.ts packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName.spec.ts",
  "patch": "diff --git a/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName.spec.ts b/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName.spec.ts\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..3e7cdab\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName.spec.ts\n@@ -0,0 +1,80 @@\n+import fs from 'node:fs'\n+import path from 'node:path'\n+import ts from 'typescript'\n+import {\n+  compileScript,\n+  compileTemplate,\n+  parse,\n+  rewriteDefault,\n+} from '@vue/compiler-sfc'\n+import * as Vue from 'vue'\n+\n+// Reproduction of: slot <template> with a name starting with \"_\" is ignored\n+// (default slot content is rendered instead) when the component using it is\n+// a sibling of a conditionally rendered (`v-if` + `#slot`) template inside\n+// another component's slot content.\n+//\n+// The three .vue files in ./underscoreSlotName are the reporter's files,\n+// unmodified (decoded from the playground link in the report). They are\n+// compiled with the in-repo @vue/compiler-sfc exactly like the Vue Vite plugin\n+// does (compileScript + compileTemplate) and mounted with the in-repo runtime.\n+\n+const fixtureDir = path.resolve(__dirname, 'underscoreSlotName')\n+const cache = new Map<string, any>()\n+\n+function loadSFC(file: string): any {\n+  if (cache.has(file)) return cache.get(file)\n+  const filename = path.join(fixtureDir, file)\n+  const source = fs.readFileSync(filename, 'utf8')\n+  const { descriptor, errors } = parse(source, { filename })\n+  if (errors.length) throw errors[0]\n+  const id = file\n+  // like @vitejs/plugin-vue: an empty <script setup> is dropped by the parser\n+  const script =\n+    descriptor.script || descriptor.scriptSetup\n+      ? compileScript(descriptor, { id, inlineTemplate: false })\n+      : { content: 'export default {}', bindings: undefined }\n+  const template = compileTemplate({\n+    source: descriptor.template!.content,\n+    filename,\n+    id,\n+    compilerOptions: { bindingMetadata: script.bindings },\n+  })\n+  if (template.errors.length) throw template.errors[0]\n+  const code =\n+    rewriteDefault(script.content, '_sfc_main', ['typescript']) +\n+    '\\n' +\n+    template.code +\n+    '\\n_sfc_main.render = render\\nexport default _sfc_main\\n'\n+  const cjs = ts.transpileModule(code, {\n+    compilerOptions: {\n+      module: ts.ModuleKind.CommonJS,\n+      target: ts.ScriptTarget.ES2022,\n+    },\n+  }).outputText\n+  const mod: any = { exports: {} }\n+  const req = (id: string) => {\n+    if (id === 'vue') return Vue\n+    if (id.endsWith('.vue')) return { default: loadSFC(id.replace('./', '')) }\n+    throw new Error(`unexpected import ${id}`)\n+  }\n+  new Function('require', 'module', 'exports', cjs)(req, mod, mod.exports)\n+  const comp = mod.exports.default\n+  cache.set(file, comp)\n+  return comp\n+}\n+\n+test('slot <template> whose name starts with \"_\" renders its content, not the fallback', () => {\n+  const App = loadSFC('App.vue')\n+  const root = document.createElement('div')\n+  Vue.createApp(App).mount(root)\n+  const html = root.innerHTML\n+\n+  // `title` (no underscore) works - control\n+  expect(html).toContain('`title` template works')\n+  expect(html).not.toContain('default slot content for `title`')\n+\n+  // `_duration` (underscore) must work the same way\n+  expect(html).toContain('`_duration` template works')\n+  expect(html).not.toContain('default slot content for `_duration`')\n+})\ndiff --git a/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName/App.vue b/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName/App.vue\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..09f7fdd\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName/App.vue\n@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@\n+<template>\n+  <BaseLayout>\n+    <template v-if=\"anyConditionCheckHereWillDo\" #randomslotname>\n+      <p>\n+        As long as we are conditionally rendering this slot, the error occurs.<br>\n+        The slot doesn't even have to exist in the component.\n+      </p>\n+    </template>\n+    \n+    <SubComponent>\n+      <template #title>\n+        <div style=\"color: green\">`title` template works</div>\n+      </template>\n+\n+      <template #_duration>\n+        <div style=\"color: green\">`_duration` template works</div>\n+      </template>\n+    </SubComponent>\n+  </BaseLayout>\n+</template>\n+\n+<script lang=\"ts\" setup>\n+  import SubComponent from './SubComponent.vue';\n+  import BaseLayout from './BaseLayout.vue';\n+\n+  const anyConditionCheckHereWillDo = true;\n+</script>\ndiff --git a/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName/BaseLayout.vue b/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName/BaseLayout.vue\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..bab7dc3\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName/BaseLayout.vue\n@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@\n+<template>\n+  <div>\n+    <slot name=\"randomslotname\"></slot>\n+    <slot></slot>\n+  </div>\n+</template>\n+\n+<script lang=\"ts\" setup>\n+</script>\ndiff --git a/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName/SubComponent.vue b/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName/SubComponent.vue\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..ca7c078\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName/SubComponent.vue\n@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@\n+<template>\n+  <slot name=\"title\">\n+    <div style=\"color: red\">This is the default slot content for `title`.<br>As long as the slotname starts with an underscore, the template doesn't work.</div>\n+  </slot>\n+\n+  <slot name=\"_duration\">\n+    <div style=\"color: red\">This is the default slot content for `_duration`.<br>As long as the slotname starts with an underscore, the template doesn't work.</div>\n+  </slot>\n+</template>\n+\n+<script lang=\"ts\" setup>\n+</script>\n"
